# Commit messages

When generating git commit messages for this repo, follow these rules.

## Before writing

- Read the full staged diff (and `git status` for new/deleted/renamed files).
- Summarize the **intent and user-visible outcome**, not a file list.
- One logical change per commit; if the diff mixes unrelated work, say so instead of blending it into one vague message.

## Format

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) with an optional scope:

```
<type>(<scope>): <short summary>

<Subheading>:
- <modification point>
- <modification point>

<Subheading>: (optional, e.g. Why)
- <reason / tradeoff / follow-up>

<optional footer>
```

The commit message body must be **plain text**. Git does not render Markdown—do not use `#`, `###`, `**`, backticks, or links in the generated commit text.

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `style`, `docs`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`, `perf`, `test`

**Scopes (examples for this project):** `astro`, `pages`, `components`, `content`, `styles`, `config`, `deps`

## Subject line

- Imperative mood: "add hero section" not "added hero section" or "adds hero section"
- ~72 characters max; no trailing period
- Specific enough that someone scanning `git log` understands what changed

## Body (use when the change is non-trivial)

- **Never** use long prose paragraphs in the body.
- **Never** use Markdown in the commit message (no `###`, headings with `#`, bold, inline code fences, or URLs as link syntax).
- Group changes with **plain-text section labels** on their own line, Title Case, ending with a colon (e.g. `Deployment:`, `UI:`, `Why:`).
- Leave a blank line after the subject, between sections, and before bullets as in the example below.
- Under each label, use `-` bullet lines—one concrete modification per bullet.
- Add a `Why:` section when reason, tradeoffs, breaking changes, or follow-up work matter.
- Keep bullets short and scannable; explain what changed, not every line of the diff.
- Do not repeat the subject line verbatim.

## Quality bar

**Avoid:**

- `update files`, `fix stuff`, `wip`, `changes`, `misc`
- Messages that only list filenames without saying what changed
- Past tense or first person ("I fixed…")
- Body text as a single long paragraph instead of labeled sections and bullets
- Markdown syntax in the commit body (`###`, `#`, `**`, backticks)

**Prefer (subject only for tiny changes):**

- `feat(pages): add project grid with filter by tag`
- `fix(styles): prevent nav overlap on mobile viewports`

**Prefer (subject + point-wise body for larger changes):**

```
feat(pages): add project grid with filter by tag

Layout:
- Add responsive grid for project cards
- Show empty state when no projects match a tag

Behavior:
- Filter projects by tag from query or control
- Preserve filter when navigating back to the page

Why:
- Keeps the projects page scannable as the portfolio grows
```

```
chore(config): add Vercel deployment settings

Deployment:
- Add vercel.json for Astro build and routing on Vercel
- Disable auto-deploy for astro-v2 git branch

Why:
- Control which branches deploy to production
```

## This project

- Stack: Astro 7, Biome for lint/format
- Prefer scopes that match `src/pages`, `src/components`, and config (`astro.config`, `biome.json`)
